Root cause:
The bug was caused by a race condition where the `server_done` flag could be set to true before the server thread had a chance to accept any incoming connections. This premature setting of the flag led to the server thread potentially exiting before it was ready, resulting in failures during the test execution.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
while (!server_done) {
```
```c
server_done = true;
```
```c
pthread_join(tid, &server_res);
```
Reason:
The race condition occurs because the `server_done` flag can be set to true before the server thread has successfully accepted a client connection. This can lead to the server thread exiting prematurely, as it may check the `server_done` flag and terminate before it has had a chance to process any incoming connections, resulting in test failures.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
while (true) {
```
```c
if (client_fd == -1 && errno == EAGAIN) {
```
Reason:
The fix involves changing the loop condition to `while (true)` to ensure that the server thread continues to attempt to accept connections indefinitely until a valid client connection is established. This prevents the premature exit of the server thread and ensures that it will only exit after successfully accepting a client or encountering an error, thus eliminating the race condition.


